## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical RN skills: building reusable components, accessibility across platforms, and theming with Appearance API, plus a small hook pattern.

## Key Concepts

- Accessibility props (accessibilityLabel, accessibilityHint, accessibilityRole)
- Theming with Appearance/useColorScheme and React Context
- Custom hook useTheme and ThemeProvider
- Performance considerations for re-renders and memoization

## Code Example

```javascript
import React, {createContext, useContext, useMemo, useState} from 'react';
import {Pressable, Text} from 'react-native';

export const ThemeContext = createContext('light');
export const useTheme = () => useContext(ThemeContext);

export function ThemeProvider({children}) {
  // Simplified example; in real code use Appearance or useColorScheme
  const [scheme] = useState('light');
  const value = useMemo(() => ({scheme}), [scheme]);
  return <ThemeContext.Provider value={value}>{children}</ThemeContext.Provider>;
}

function Card({title, price}) {
  const {scheme} = useTheme();
  const bg = scheme === 'dark' ? '#222' : '#fff';
  return (
    <Pressable accessibilityLabel={title}
               accessibilityHint="View details"
               accessibilityRole="button"
               style={{backgroundColor: bg}}>
      <Text>{title}</Text>
      <Text>{price}</Text>
    </Pressable>
  );
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test accessibility coverage across iOS and Android?
- How would you extend theming to allow user-selected custom colors without breaking contrast?

## Key Concepts
- **Flexbox Layout**: Primary responsive design tool
- **Dimensions API**: Screen size detection with event listeners
- **Safe Area Handling**: Notch and home indicator accommodation
- **Platform Differences**: iOS vs Android variations

## Implementation
```javascript
import { Dimensions } from 'react-native';

// Reactive orientation handling
const [dimensions, setDimensions] = useState(Dimensions.get('window'));

useEffect(() => {
  const subscription = Dimensions.addEventListener('change', ({ window }) => {
    setDimensions(window);
  });
  return () => subscription?.remove();
}, []);

const isLandscape = dimensions.width > dimensions.height;
```

## Safe Area Handling
```javascript
import { SafeAreaProvider, useSafeAreaInsets } from 'react-native-safe-area-context';

// Wrap your root component
function App() {
  return (
    <SafeAreaProvider>
      <MainApp />
    </SafeAreaProvider>
  );
}

// Use in components
function ScreenContent() {
  const insets = useSafeAreaInsets();
  return (
    <View style={{ paddingTop: insets.top, paddingBottom: insets.bottom }}>
      {/* content */}
    </View>
  );
}
```

## Best Practices
- Use Flexbox and relative units over fixed pixels
- Implement safe area insets to handle notches and home indicators
- Use `Dimensions.addEventListener` for reactive orientation changes (hooks are static)
- Test on various device ratios and notch configurations
- Consider platform-specific safe area requirements

